  "conclusion": "DMEM ranks #2 overall but AMEM (#1) significantly beats it (DM=+4.35, Harvey PASS). QLIKE ranking: AMEM > DMEM > GJR > MEM > HAR-ABS. Despite +122 NLL improvement in-sample (7 vs 5 params), DMEM loses OOS to simpler AMEM. Key finding: DMEM wins in calm regime (QLIKE 1.18 vs 1.22) but loses badly in crisis (0.41 vs 0.37) — the extra τ_t estimation noise hurts when volatility spikes. AMEM's high β=0.88 implicitly captures long-memory without explicit decomposition. The α_g=0 in DMEM (short-run ARCH collapsed to zero) suggests the model struggles to separate components cleanly.",
